{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792846293,"nonce":"I4roXrJRarPemnyn1phwusvmLbg=","title":"Debug shell (attach / debug-pod) into a step Pod should be a step-up crown jewel","message":"`GET /v1/runs/{id}/steps/{step}/attach` and `GET /v1/runs/{id}/steps/{step}/debug-pod` open a WebSocket exec into a step Pod. They need Administer, but under ADR-0073 they are classified READ (they are GETs, so the step-up guard never consults them): no StepUpConfirmation is asked.\n\nAn exec into a step Pod can read the Pod's environment, which today includes secrets as plain env (bcf2c11), and can act with the Pod's credentials. That is at least as sensitive as a secret write, which IS a crown jewel.\n\nProposal: classify both as CrownJewel(Window) with an explicit guard hook for these GETs (the guard currently passes every GET untouched — add a per-route opt-in for side-effecting GETs, and keep the table-driven test exhaustive over them). Owner decision: window or always-ask.\n\nFound in the ADR-0073 step-up build (AFK run 20261024-1301; plan §1 AMBIG list, ADR-0073 Follow-ups \"not yet ticketed\"); branch feat/step-up.","files":null}]}